# Environment files
#
# NOTE: .env, .env.development, .env.staging and .env.production are ALREADY
# tracked. A .gitignore rule does not untrack a file, so these four keep being
# committed and the build keeps working. See docs/env-handling.md for why they
# have not been removed and what has to happen first.
#
# What this rule DOES do: stop any NEW env file (.env.local, .env.secrets, a
# colleague's scratch copy) from being committed by accident. Server-side code
# reads real secrets — SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, STRIPE_LIVE_API_KEY,
# VAPI_SERVER_SECRET — and vite.config.ts loads every var from these files into
# process.env, so one pasted secret would otherwise land in git silently.
.env*
!.env.example

# Wrangler / Cloudflare
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

